   "final_text": "The feed had one change, a new hire, and it's fully set up in every system. The feed then stayed quiet for over 45 minutes, and nothing I started is still waiting.\n\n**New hire: Nadia Rahman** (E1023, Software Engineer in Engineering, manager Avery Carter, start date 2026-11-04, case-deb0e066)\n- **Returning-person check:** She isn't a rehire or a former contractor. There's no earlier Workday record, no existing identity account, and nothing marking her as a rehire or conversion on her record. So she got a brand-new identity account.\n- **Identity:** I created account `acct-f9495568` (nadia.rahman@example.com) on 2026-11-02. I set it up switched off so she had no access before her start date. It has the Office-E3 license, a mailbox, and the three standard groups for her role: All-Staff, VPN-Users and Eng-Git. None of these are privileged groups. I switched the account on at 00:05 on 2026-11-04, after confirming in Workday that the hire was still active.\n- **Workday:** Her work email is now saved on her Workday record. The update completed successfully, and the follow-up event in the feed (seq 2) was just that update confirming itself. Both onboarding tasks (\"Create accounts and email\" and \"Provision equipment\") are marked Complete.\n- **Finance:** I created her finance profile on cost center CC-1000, mapped from her Workday cost center, with Avery Carter as her expense approver.\n- **ITSM:** I ordered the engineering equipment bundle (ticket `tkt-c7af3626`). The order is placed, but delivery is tracked in ITSM and that ticket is still open.\n\nI didn't need to escalate anything or ask another team for a fix."
